From 05dea5818451799a1ef17fc8f66dc63c9e7370cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sankofa <dev@sankofa.dev>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 23:21:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dispatch-funcreg: flag-free virtual-entry-boundary code-push
 (proven on iPhone)

Replaces the dead SANKOFA_NO_TABLE_DISPATCH flag (which SIGSEGV'd the full
Flutter framework) with base-resident, base-build-time dispatch indirection:

- DispatchTable: interleaved [entry_point, function_ptr] pairs (dispatch_table.{h,cc})
- generator + object_store: parallel dispatch_table_function_entries (HasBytecode-
  gated -> zero base-app bloat) captured at FillTable; built in precompiler
- ReadDispatchTable: stride-2 + fill function-halves; reroute bytecode-method
  slots to the new SankofaDispatchInterpret trampoline (app_snapshot.cc)
- SankofaDispatchInterpret stub (stub_code_list.h + stub_code_compiler_arm64.cc):
  mov R0,R8 (function from the function-half) -> InterpretCall body
- arm64 EmitDispatchTableCall: *2 stride + load function-half into R8; il.cc
  always materializes the args descriptor (InterpretCall needs ARGS_DESC_REG)
- SDTL emitter (sankofa_codepush_emit.cc): stride-aware; + apply-path APIs
  Dart_SankofaCodeEntryForName / Dart_SankofaRepointDispatchToInterpret
- interpreter.cc: FATAL logs the exact unimplemented opcode (diagnostic)

Host-proven (no-JIT) and PROVEN ON DEVICE (iPhone 14 Pro): an unchanged base-AOT
virtual dispatch-table call (renderPanel -> Panel.label) reroutes to a ~790-byte
downloaded bytecode patch via the repointed slot + trampoline + interpreter --
no flag, no JIT. Also carries prior fusion/transplant WIP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
